abstract: >
  This monograph examines how technology has consistently shaped human hierarchy
  and national power. From early tools to modern AI, engineering capacity—not
  ideology—is treated as a central constraint on geopolitical strength. It
  analyzes global STEM talent, platform ecosystems such as TikTok and Douyin,
  and a revised map of system-builders, specialized chokepoint builders,
  system-consumers, and system-dependents.
